# Scholarium Codebase Refactor Plan

This plan outlines a series of safe refactors to improve the maintainability, readability, and professional structure of the Scholarium codebase.

## Goal
Clean up and restructure the codebase without changing functionality, output, UX behavior, business logic, model behavior, or API contracts.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I will be extracting logic into new files (e.g., `llm_service.py`, `AssessmentComponent.jsx`). This changes the internal file structure but not the external behavior.

## Proposed Changes

### [Backend] Agent Module

#### [MODIFY] [agent_engine.py](file:///c:/Users/saivi/Downloads/Scholarium/backend/agent/agent_engine.py)
- Remove low-level LLM call logic (`call_claude`, `call_gemini`, `call_llm`).
- Remove JSON parsing logic (`_parse_json`).
- Remove redundant `raise e` and internal imports.
- Focus this file on domain-specific AI logic (roadmap generation, subtopic expansion, etc.).

#### [NEW] [llm_service.py](file:///c:/Users/saivi/Downloads/Scholarium/backend/agent/llm_service.py)
- Centralize LLM provider setup (Anthropic, Gemini).
- Implement `call_llm` with integrated caching and retry logic.
- Define a custom `RateLimitError` here.

#### [NEW] [utils.py](file:///c:/Users/saivi/Downloads/Scholarium/backend/agent/utils.py)
- Move `_parse_json` and other common utilities here.

#### [MODIFY] [views.py](file:///c:/Users/saivi/Downloads/Scholarium/backend/agent/views.py)
- Remove duplicate `find_similar_goal`.
- Clean up redundant imports.
- Improve error handling consistency.

